Z||000000||ndm86||01-09-2001||06:42 AM||||I see that the rear bushings are not available for the 88's except in urethane, I have tried the Fiero store and they state that none are available for stock replacement. By examining my spare rear trailing arms I have seen that Clevite supplied the bushings but there is no part # only mold #'s. Does anyone have contacts at Clevite to cross refrence the #'s in there database? I find it real hard to believe that these parts are Fiero specific with the spacers involved and the money crunching that GM likes to do, and help would be appreciated! Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||gixxer||01-09-2001||06:31 PM||||Can't answer your question about the bushing cross reference.<BR>However, I installed the urethane rear suspension Prothane kit on my '88 recently and am pleased with the outcome. Replacing the stock bushes on only the 4 lateral links gave me a very good ride. I hesitate to use the urethane stuff on the fore/aft links. I believe that would directly influence the ride quality over sharp bumps, as the suspension needs to deflect substantially rearward initially, then upwards as well.<BR>In the near future I plan to install lube fittings on all joints as I did on my Honda. <BR>Good luck with your quest. ||||reg||1
